### [The ABI Mapper]($section.id('2025-07-08T00:00:00').data('author','xq'))

I'm working on the so called ABI mapper, a tool that converts a DSL containing
the system call interface of Ashet OS into actual code.

The new changes are supporting non-C ABI compatible types like Zig-style slices (pointers + length) and options.

> []($block.attrs('pictures'))
> []($image.siteAsset('img/devlog/2025/2025-07-08_abi-mapper-1.webp').linked(true))
> []($image.siteAsset('img/devlog/2025/2025-07-08_abi-mapper-2.webp').linked(true))
> []($image.siteAsset('img/devlog/2025/2025-07-08_abi-mapper-3.webp').linked(true))

I'm slowly getting back to where I came from, but the ABI definition is now so much cleaner now.

